.Dd October 24, 2026
.Dt AUGITE-INDEX 1
.Os Augite DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm augite-index
.Nd generate an index of Git repositories
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "augite index"
.Oo
.Fl o
.Ar dir No \&|
.Fl "-output"
.Ar dir
.Oc
.Ar repo-dir
.No ...
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm "augite index"
writes an index page listing the repositories given as arguments.
Each entry shows the repository’s name,
description and latest commit date.
Descriptions can be set with
.Xr augite-setup 1 .
.Pp
The command writes
.Ql "index\&.html"
and
.Ql "style\&.css"
to the output directory,
creating the directory if necessary.
Existing files at those paths are replaced.
The default output directory is the current directory.
.Pp
Each entry links to a subdirectory named after the repository,
with any trailing
.Ql "\&.git"
removed.
For example,
a repository at
.Eo
.Pa /var/git/engine.git
.Ec
links to
.Eo
.Pa engine/
.Ec
beside the index page.
Generate each repository’s pages separately with
.Xr augite-repo 1
in the matching subdirectory.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl o ,
.Fl "-output"
.Ar dir
.Xc
Writes the index and stylesheet to
.Ar dir
instead of the current directory.
.It Xo
.Fl h ,
.Fl "-help"
.Xc
Prints a usage summary and exits.
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate two repository sites and an index linking to both:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ augite repo -o public/engine /var/git/engine\&.git
$ augite repo -o public/notes /var/git/notes\&.git
$ augite index -o public /var/git/engine\&.git /var/git/notes\&.git
.Ed
.Pp
The index is written to
.Eo
.Pa public/index.html
.Ec .
Each repository’s
.Ql "logo\&.png"
is used beside its entry;
Augite does not create these images.
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr augite 1 ,
.Xr augite-repo 1 ,
.Xr augite-setup 1
.
